rename andes-sim -> andesim; clean up the run CLI surface

This session's product/CLI changes. They are entangled across the same
driver files, so they land as one commit rather than per-feature:

- Rename the product andes-sim -> andesim: the ./andesim launcher,
  build/andesim, CMake targets, error/help text, and the user ABI
  (-specs=andesim.specs, andesim.ld, <andesim/ROI.h>, -landesim_runtime,
  andesim_ROI_begin/end) plus env vars (ANDES_SIM_* -> ANDESIM_*). The
  internal C++ namespace andes_sim and the tests/andes_sim/ dir are
  intentionally kept.
- run: surface `doctor` in the release --help (was dev-only).
- run: rename --model -> --mode (clean break; the Cli::model field and
  the "model" concept / `list models` stay).
- run: document --gdb / --gdb-port / --verify in `run --help`.
- run: drop `icount` from --trigger (marker|pc only); the icount
  measurement mechanism stays in the plan layer for SimPoint.

Structural (rename) + behavioral (CLI surface, ABI). Driver unit tests
and the marker/pc shell tests pass; docs and notebooks updated.

Note: cmd_run.cpp also carries a pre-existing, unrelated run_cycle_gdb
change (drop -S, add -I virtual_dmi.cfg) that was already in the working
tree and overlaps the renamed lines, so it could not be split out.

